ERROR    FMT001  lib/l10n/app_de.arb:4  Placeholder mismatch
         "booksOnShelf" in German (de) uses {regal}, which the source text does not have
         Fix: Use the placeholder names of the template message; every placeholder needs a
         declaration in the template's "@key" metadata.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#fmt001

WARNING  FMT002  lib/l10n/app_de.arb:4  Placeholder dropped
         "booksOnShelf" in German (de) leaves out {shelf} of the source text
         Fix: Add the placeholder to the translation. Plural forms for one or two items may leave
         out the number on purpose; this rule does not report those.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#fmt002

INFO     KEY003  lib/l10n/app_en.arb:28  Unused key
         "syncFailed" is not mentioned in any source file
         Fix: Delete the message from every ARB file, or ignore it in .globallingo.json if it is
         used outside lib/.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#key003

WARNING  PLU001  lib/l10n/app_pl.arb:4  Missing plural form
         "booksOnShelf" in Polish (pl) has no plural forms for few (e.g. 2, 3, 4), many (e.g. 0, 5,
         6)
         Fix: Add the missing category to the plural in this locale's message, e.g. few{…}.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#plu001

INFO     MIS004  lib/l10n/app_pl.arb:6  Same as the source
         The Polish (pl) translation of "deleteAll" is the same as the source text
         Fix: Translate it, or ignore the key in .globallingo.json when the text is the same in both
         languages (brand names, "OK").
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#mis004

ERROR    MIS001  lib/l10n/app_tr.arb  Missing translation
         "syncFailed" has no Turkish (tr) translation
         Fix: Add the key to this locale's ARB file. Until then gen_l10n uses the template's message
         for it.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#mis001

WARNING  HCS001  lib/main.dart:16  Hard-coded UI text
         "Bookshelf" is shown to the user but is not localized
         Fix: Add the text to the template ARB file and read it through the generated class, e.g.
         AppLocalizations.of(context)!.title.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#hcs001

WARNING  TRI003  lib/main.dart:49  Translated text cased without the locale
         Translated text is changed with toUpperCase(), which ignores the locale; Turkish and
         Azerbaijani need İ and ı
         Fix: Dart's toUpperCase() ignores the locale. Put the upper-case text in the ARB file as
         its own message, so the Turkish translator writes İ.
         https://github.com/muhittincamdali/GlobalLingo/blob/master/docs/rules.md#tri003

